 "caveats": [
  "NAV is as-collected: a later pull may restate it, and a restated NAV moves the whole series by that revision (the raw cache is regenerable, the published history CSV is this session's reading).",
  "A cross-border (QDII) NAV is stamped on the overseas close, so part of every reading is the overseas move since that stamp -- the lag ladder prices how much of the reading that offset can shift.",
  "A限购 fund can stay expensive for years: a high percentile is a reading, not a sell order.",
  "A rank counts sessions, and a session whose NAV stamp repeats the previous valuation carries no new number -- the second rank drops those rows and the calendars in hand only explain them.",
  "The second rank does NOT drop a session whose NAV moved only slightly (a distribution or a share conversion moves the number without moving the basket). Those rows are measured on their own face (results/etf_premium/PREMIUM-SUBSCRIPTION.json), which counts the one-row suspension runs; this face does not re-decide them.",
  "The panel close is not the price the sheet pays; the sheet pays the next open plus slippage (tracked on the punctuality faces).",
  "This rank is read at the ticket's own session: bars the panel holds past that session are counted on `panel.bars_beyond_session` and excluded, so a panel that moves on overnight cannot reprice a sheet that has not moved."
 ],
